{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-flavor-mass-splitting-bound","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:flavor-mass-splitting-bound","kind":"theorem","title":"Two-sided substrate bound on the dressed-quark splitting","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-flavor-split-substrate-mass"],"tags":["flavor","dressing","quark-mass","substrate-bound","splitting-only"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.FlavorDressing.flavor_mass_splitting_bound","text":"flavor-mass-splitting-bound.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:flavor-mass-splitting-bound\"></a><p><strong>Conditional on <a href=\"#conj:flavor-split-substrate-mass\" data-at=\"mass-theory/mass-algebraic-consolidated/mass-algebraic-transfer-skein\">the substrate flavor split conjecture</a>.</strong> The closed form for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu_{\\mathfrak{d}} - \\mu_{\\mathfrak{u}}</code> is <a href=\"#prop:flavor-dressed-mass-from-substrate-split\" data-at=\"mass-theory/alpha-k-procedure\">derived</a> from that conjecture and the nucleon form of the pair Skein mass formula, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_N = (m_{\\mathfrak{p}} + m_{\\mathfrak{n}})/2</code>.</p>\n<p><em>For substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code>, the down-up splitting satisfies the two-sided bound:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  0 \\;&#x3C;\\; \\mu_{\\mathfrak{d}} - \\mu_{\\mathfrak{u}}\n  \\;&#x3C;\\; M_N \\cdot \\hbar_q^2 \\cdot h_q \\cdot [2]_q,</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q = (q - 1)/q</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h_q = q - q^{-1}</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_q = q + q^{-1}</code>.</em></p>\n<p>The bound is on the difference rather than the individual masses, which isolates the substrate-derivable quantity from the CODATA-anchored mean.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flavor-mass-splitting-bound.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"13.28.2","page":"b/thm-flavor-mass-splitting-bound","qa":{"counts":{"pass":94,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":26,"unknown":0,"stale":95},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.FlavorDressing.flavor_mass_splitting_bound","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/FlavorMassSplittingBound.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
